    },
    "body": "## Summary\n- Refactors `ValidAdminEndpointAccessHandler` to use file-scoped namespace, focused private methods, and clearer control flow aligned with other refactored auth handlers.\n- Introduces `AdminApiAuthHelpers` to centralize bearer-token extraction, tenant ID resolution, authentication short-circuit checks, and tenant-context population shared with the authorization path.\n- Preserves existing authorization behavior, including the authentication short-circuit, `TenantNotFoundException` propagation, and sanitized logging.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `dotnet build XiansAi.Server.Src/XiansAi.Server.csproj` succeeds with no warnings\n- [ ] Verify Admin API requests with a valid API key still authorize successfully\n- [ ] Verify requests where authentication already populated `ITenantContext` skip redundant resolution\n- [ ] Verify invalid/missing bearer tokens still fail authorization\n- [ ] Verify SysAdmin cross-tenant access and TenantAdmin tenant scoping still behave as before\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
